{"name":"Pickled Salmon","hex":"#ff6655","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pickled","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of pickle"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Preserved by pickling.","Drunk."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pickled"},{"term":"salmon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of several species of fish, typically of the Salmoninae subfamily, brownish above with silvery sides and delicate pinkish-orange flesh; they ascend rivers to spawn.","A meal or dish made from this fish."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a pale pinkish-orange colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/salmon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pickling","blocks":[{"text":"Pickling is the process of preserving or extending the shelf life of food by either anaerobic fermentation in brine or immersion in vinegar. The pickling procedure typically affects the food's texture and flavor. The resulting food is called a pickle, or, if named, the name is prefaced with the word \"pickled\". Foods that are pickled include vegetables, fruits, mushrooms, meats, fish, dairy and eggs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Gherkins_and_Onions.JPG/330px-Gherkins_and_Onions.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pickling","wikidata":"Q1503967"},{"title":"Salmon","blocks":[{"text":"Salmon are any of several commercially important species of ray-finned fish that can live in either freshwater or saltwater from the genera Salmo and Oncorhynchus of the family Salmonidae, native to tributaries of the North Atlantic (Salmo) and North Pacific (Oncorhynchus) basins. Salmon is a colloquial or common name used for fish in this group, but is not a scientific name. Other closely related fish in the same family include trout, char, grayling, whitefish, lenok and taimen, all coldwater fish of the subarctic and cooler temperate regions with some sporadic endorheic populations in Central Asia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Salmo_salar.jpg/330px-Salmo_salar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salmon","wikidata":"Q2796766"},{"title":"Salmon (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Salmon is a warm color ranging from light orange to pink, named after the color of salmon flesh."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/SockeyeMaleCloseup_%2814522094556%29.jpg/330px-SockeyeMaleCloseup_%2814522094556%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salmon_(color)","wikidata":"Q2015138"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Tursucu_Sahne_sokak_beyoglu_Istanbul_0644.jpg/500px-Tursucu_Sahne_sokak_beyoglu_Istanbul_0644.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Tursucu_Sahne_sokak_beyoglu_Istanbul_0644.jpg/500px-Tursucu_Sahne_sokak_beyoglu_Istanbul_0644.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Torshi, traditional pickles in Southeast Europe, West Asia and Northern Africa","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATursucu_Sahne_sokak_beyoglu_Istanbul_0644.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/PikiWiki_Israel_39626_Cities_in_Israel.JPG/500px-PikiWiki_Israel_39626_Cities_in_Israel.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/PikiWiki_Israel_39626_Cities_in_Israel.JPG/1280px-PikiWiki_Israel_39626_Cities_in_Israel.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/PikiWiki_Israel_39626_Cities_i